  "term": "eszopiclone",
  "definition": "Eszopiclone is a nonbenzodiazepine sedative-hypnotic drug used to promote sleep. It acts on the GABA-A receptor complex in the central nervous system, increasing inhibitory signaling that reduces neuronal activity and helps induce sleep, with little significant anxiety-reducing effect.",
